Parity reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity):
  id        = vehicleId ?? vehicles[0].id ?? null  (default-vehicle resolution at the source seam)
  3 queries = useDashboardStats() + useVehicleStateMachine(id) + useStateTimeline(id), coalesced:
              updatedAt = max(dataUpdatedAt) · isFetching/isStale/isError = OR · isLoading=stats||fsm ·
              hasData = stats.data != null
  statItems = Vehicles / Trips / Charge Sessions (fmtInt = en_US grouped, 0 frac, half-away-from-zero)
              + FSM State (raw value, web StatCard shows the unformatted state string)
  fsmState  = fsm.data?.state ?? '—'   (em-dash fallback, neutral tone)
  badge tone= ported from web VEHICLE_STATE_ENTRIES variant table (types/fsm/vehicle.ts):
              online/driving=success · charging=warning · parked/updating=info · asleep=neutral ·
              offline=danger · unknown=neutral.   Current-State label uses the vehicle.state.{state}
              catalog key (web VEHICLE_STATE_LABELS); unknown states capitalize-first (CSS capitalize parity).
  layouts   = compact(cols<=1): big fmtInt(totalTrips) + "active"; standard(cols 2): 2-col grid +
              "Current State" StatusBadge; wide(cols>=3): + "Recent Transitions" = transitions.slice(0,5).

